## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of Kleene 3-valued semantics, constraint propagation, and backtracking strategy in a practical policy engine scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene 3-valued logic (T > U > F)
- Propagation and backtracking on partial assignments
- Constraint forms: implication, conjunction, disjunction

## Code Example
```javascript
// Kleene 3-valued logic: F=0, U=1, T=2
const V = {F:0, U:1, T:2};
const not = v => (v===V.T?V.F:(v===V.F?V.T:V.U));
const and = (a,b)=> Math.min(a,b);
const or  = (a,b)=> Math.max(a,b);
const implies = (a,b)=> or(not(a), b);
function evalConstraints(I1,I2,I3,I4){
  const c1 = implies(or(I1, not(I2)), I3);
  const c2 = implies(and(I2,I4), not(I1));
  const c3 = or(and(I1,I3), I4);
  return [c1,c2,c3];
}
```

